start": 220, "notes": ["«علي يعني ابن مسهر» is read as «علي» with the editor's gloss left out. Six routes: five heads (Ali b. Hujr; Abu Kurayb; Abu Bakr; Abu Kurayb again; Ibn Numayr; and Amr al-Naqid with Wakii) meet at Hisham and «بهذا الإسناد», which are written once and shared. «وفي حديث أبي أسامة إذا طلع الفجر» is a variant note in the saying, not a route. The offsets for this long opening are approximate."]}
